<title>GERMANY: German authority delays Hochtief-Holzmann study.</title>
<headline>German authority delays Hochtief-Holzmann study.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cartel authorities said on Wednesday they had put back the first hearings over an increase in cooperation between German builders Hochtief AG and Philipp Holzmann AG until April 9.</p>
<p>The hearings were due to start on February 5. Hochtief is seeking to increase its stake in Holzmann from 20 percent to around 35 percent, and the two have indicated plans to collaborate more closely with each other on building projects.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
